    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d117">

                <pb facs="0292" n="204" xml:id="pg204"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.G Women’s Rights/17: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chairman of the
                        American Delegation</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hull</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-12-20T16:00:00-05:00">December 20, 1933—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>106. My 105, December 20, 3 p.m. For your information the National Woman’s Party
                    has just received a telegram from Miss Doris Stevens announcing that the United
                    States will sign the Treaty on Nationality. Neither the White House nor the
                    State Department is making any official statement in this regard awaiting your
                    action.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
